Step 1: Create New Project Folder
Shell
mkdir -p /opt/rag-project
cd /opt/rag-project

Verify:

Shell
pwd

Output:

Plain Text
/opt/rag-project
Step 2: Create Dedicated Network
Shell
docker network create rag-net

Verify:

Shell
docker network ls

Output:

Plain Text
rag-net
Step 3: Create PostgreSQL Container
Shell
docker run -d \
--name rag-postgres \
--network rag-net \
-e POSTGRES_USER=admin \
-e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=admin123 \
-e POSTGRES_DB=ragdb \
-p 5433:5432 \
postgres:16

Check:

Shell
docker ps

Expected:

Plain Text
rag-postgres
0.0.0.0:5433->5432
Step 4: Verify PostgreSQL
Shell
docker logs rag-postgres
 

Should show:

Plain Text
database system is ready to accept connections
Step 5: Create Ollama Container

If running Ollama in Docker:

Shell
docker run -d \
--name rag-ollama \
--network rag-net \
-p 11434:11434 \
ollama/ollama

Check:

Shell
docker ps
Step 6: Download Qwen Model

Enter container:

Shell
docker exec -it rag-ollama bash

Pull model:

Shell
ollama pull qwen2.5

Verify:

Shell
ollama list

Exit:

Shell
exit
Step 7: Prepare FastAPI Project

Go to project:

Shell
cd ~/rag_project
 

Files:

Plain Text
main.py
Dockerfile
requirements.txt
runbooks/
Step 8: Build Image
Shell
docker build -t rag-fastapi:v1 .

Verify:

Shell
docker images

Expected:

Plain Text
rag-fastapi v1
Step 9: Remove Old Failed Container

You currently have:

Plain Text
rag_api (Created)

Remove:

Shell
docker rm -f rag_api

Verify:

Shell
docker ps -a

Should disappear.

Step 10: Run FastAPI on Port 8001
Shell
docker run -d \
--name rag-fastapi \
--network rag-net \
-p 8001:8000 \
rag-fastapi:v1

Check:

Shell
docker ps

Expected:

Plain Text
rag-fastapi
0.0.0.0:8001->8000
Step 11: Check Logs
Shell
docker logs rag-fastapi
 

Expected:

Plain Text
Uvicorn running on http://0.0.0.0:8000
Step 12: Test API
Shell
curl http://localhost:8001/docs

Browser:

Plain Text
http://SERVER-IP:8001/docs
Step 13: Connect FastAPI to PostgreSQL

In your Python code:

Python
DATABASE_URL = "postgresql://admin:admin123@rag-postgres:5432/ragdb"

Notice:

Plain Text
rag-postgres

is the container name inside rag-net.

Step 14: Connect FastAPI to Ollama

If Ollama is containerized:

Python
OLLAMA_URL = "http://rag-ollama:11434"

If Ollama runs directly on VM:

Python
OLLAMA_URL = "http://host.docker.internal:11434"
Step 15: Verify Isolation

Check networks:

Shell
docker network inspect rag-net

Should show:

Plain Text
rag-fastapi
rag-postgres
rag-ollama

Only Project 2 containers.

Final Layout
Plain Text
VM
│
├── PROJECT 1
│ ├── FastAPI :8000
│ ├── Grafana :3000
│ ├── Prometheus :9090
│ └── NodeExporter :9100
│
└── PROJECT 2
├── FastAPI :8001
├── PostgreSQL :5433
├── Ollama :11434
└── ChromaDB : Internal
Useful Commands

See all containers:

Shell
docker ps

See all networks:

Shell
docker network ls

See container logs:

Shell
docker logs rag-fastapi

Enter container:

Shell
docker exec -it rag-fastapi bash

Stop Project 2:

Shell
docker stop rag-fastapi rag-postgres rag-ollama

Start Project 2:

Shell
docker start rag-fastapi rag-postgres rag-ollama

This gives you two completely independent projects on the same VM without port conflicts.




